{:edb/db-before-t 1231 :edb/db-after-t 1232 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534544 50 #inst "2026-10-07T21:53:25.018Z" 13194139534544 true] [17592186157328 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293956 13194139534544 true] [17592186157328 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293963 13194139534544 true] [17592186157328 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293980 13194139534544 true] [17592186157329 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293970 13194139534544 true] [17592186157329 1020 #edb/ref 17592186293977 13194139534544 true] [17592186293956 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293957 13194139534544 true] [17592186293956 1089 "q-115263" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293956 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534544 true] [17592186293956 1100 "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-5}^{5}\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x$" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293956 1113 #uuid "003716db-57a2-50a0-93b9-fabd05c60e4f" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293956 1145 "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\frac{(-x)}{1+(-x)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{5}\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =(-x)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-g(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)$ is an odd function, but integral III is not of the form ${\\int }_{-a}^{a}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ since the upper and lower limits are not opposites. Therefore, we cannot use symmetry to simplify the integral.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293958 13194139534544 true] [17592186293957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293959 13194139534544 true] [17592186293957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293960 13194139534544 true] [17592186293957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293961 13194139534544 true] [17592186293957 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293962 13194139534544 true] [17592186293957 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534544 true] [17592186293957 1041 "selection" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293957 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293961 13194139534544 true] [17592186293957 1110 #uuid "a16eaefb-19e8-59da-a5d0-20d0936fb4d8" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293958 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293958 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293958 1111 #uuid "3a260ab7-ec4e-5be6-a23b-0ef49fbb9037" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293959 1034 "I only" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293959 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293959 1111 #uuid "454718fd-cec3-5314-bc59-0ef0925bb14a" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293960 1034 "III only" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293960 1111 #uuid "ac35a606-c82a-58f9-a12e-7f9263cb1fcb" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293961 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293961 1111 #uuid "22904e93-3bc2-524f-bd1d-dec471d5c814" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293962 1034 "II only" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293962 1111 #uuid "36512373-978c-5e04-b699-6cc3ed57ebf5" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293963 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293964 13194139534544 true] [17592186293963 1089 "q-115275" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293963 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534544 true] [17592186293963 1100 "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /4}{sin}^{5}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}+{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x$" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293963 1113 #uuid "e095d55a-119e-5605-a59e-6bf7a4f824f8" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293963 1145 "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)={sin}^{5}⁡x$ is an odd function, but integral I is not of the form ${\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ since the upper and lower limits are not opposites. Therefore, we cannot use symmetry to simplify the integral.\n\n- The function $g(x)={x}^{3}+{x}^{5}$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =(-x)^{3}+(-x)^{5} \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}+(-{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-{x}^{5} \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}+{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =-g(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}+{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)={x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-x) & =(-x)^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(-x)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x) \\\\  & =-h(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293965 13194139534544 true] [17592186293964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293966 13194139534544 true] [17592186293964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293967 13194139534544 true] [17592186293964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293968 13194139534544 true] [17592186293964 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293969 13194139534544 true] [17592186293964 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534544 true] [17592186293964 1041 "selection" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293964 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293965 13194139534544 true] [17592186293964 1110 #uuid "963373fb-92fc-5011-bc4c-244978d19c6d" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293965 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293965 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293965 1111 #uuid "93bf8ee5-8b75-5a6a-9d29-a37bb7dfc3e3" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293966 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293966 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293966 1111 #uuid "6a3b6897-a643-5898-a15e-295325df1025" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293967 1034 "III only" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293967 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293967 1111 #uuid "4a241514-f9aa-5c04-875b-aa629a2d6ac6" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293968 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293968 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293968 1111 #uuid "8d56f6ab-fe15-552d-b7bc-45f28a9bb60c" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293969 1034 "II only" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293969 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534544 true] [17592186293969 1111 #uuid "9d9d61b8-8141-5048-b2b2-ef029037ccd6" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293970 1017 #edb/ref 17592186293971 13194139534544 true] [17592186293970 1089 "q-156191" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293970 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534544 true] [17592186293970 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{-e}^{0}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x=A,$ what is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293970 1113 #uuid "3923b7ab-8feb-5de3-adf5-945f64f8af6d" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293970 1145 "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)={e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =({e}^{-x}-{e}^{-(-x)}) \\\\  & =({e}^{-x}-{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)={e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-e}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-e}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-e}^{0}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ A+{\\int }_{0}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{e}({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})\\,\\text{d}x & =-A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293972 13194139534544 true] [17592186293971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293973 13194139534544 true] [17592186293971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293974 13194139534544 true] [17592186293971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293975 13194139534544 true] [17592186293971 1000 #edb/ref 17592186293976 13194139534544 true] [17592186293971 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534544 true] [17592186293971 1041 "selection" 13194139534544 true] [17592186293971 1104 #edb/ref 17592186293974 13194139534544 true] [17592186293971 1110 #uuid "4a96d4ac-7bf1-5b43-8